5. VERDICT
============================================================================================

   Q1a  outward finger thickness t = 19.76 mm per side
        zero-thickness alignment window : 6.94 mm
        window with the real fingers    : -32.58 mm   (= 6.94 - 2t)
        -> STRATEGY A (pair-capture) IS DEAD. The fingers are too thick for
           any placement that puts both of them in free gaps. No open-gripper
           placement at the nominal row is collision-free, at any alignment.
        -> each free gap would have to widen by 17.29 mm (to 29.29 mm) for a 2 mm-tolerance window.

   Q1b  closed-gripper blade width = 38.59 mm
        vs nominal 12 mm gap   : does NOT fit (margin -26.59 mm)
        vs worst measured 7 mm : does NOT fit (margin -31.59 mm)
        vs Tight-v0 6 mm       : does NOT fit (margin -32.59 mm)
        A blade that fits can be inserted BETWEEN blocks (strategies C/D/E).
        A blade that does not fit can still push a block's exposed face.

   Q5   block mu_s = 0.9, table mu_s = 1.0  [read off the table's bound material]
        PhysX combines by AVERAGE by default -> effective mu = 0.950
        This is NOT the 0.9 the analysis assumed. Every h_crit moves:
        tip-vs-slide across the row (b=30 mm): 15.79 mm   (was 16.67 mm at mu=0.9)
        tip-vs-slide along the row  (b=36 mm): 18.95 mm   (was 20.00 mm at mu=0.9)

   Q1c  at the HOME wrist pose the lowest finger geometry sits 93.74 mm below the TCP.
        That drop is orientation-dependent, so it is NOT a contact height. The
        real number is P02's achieved `low_z` at a grasp-height pose; this run
        only bounds the jaw's own extent. Do not compare it to h_crit here.

